    "body": "Related fix in PR #1615 (#1603): a stock-source 2D Pocket / Adaptive / Offset that cuts a part in the setup now carries a blocking gouge on the operation itself (`operation::keep_law`), so it no longer rides on `verify`'s program sim alone and cannot post on a turned stock. This issue's generate-side asks (rough the stock minus the part; say when a band narrower than the tool is skipped) are not changed by that PR.",
